  "claim": "One57 was the tallest building in Manhattan until the completion of an even taller building. That building is taller than the building that is the site of the former Loew's State Theatre (New York City) built in 1969.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Bertelsmann Building. Sentence: The former Bertelsmann Building, now known as 1540 Broadway, is a 44-story, 733 foot (223 m) office tower in Times Square in Manhattan, New York City, standing at West 45th Street.\nPage: 432 Park Avenue. Sentence: 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City that overlooks Central Park.\nPage: 432 Park Avenue. Sentence: Originally proposed to be 1300 ft in 2011, the structure topped out at 1396 ft .\nPage: Loew's State Theatre (New York City). Sentence: It closed on February 19, 1987, and it is now the site of the Bertelsmann Building.\nPage: One57. Sentence: Upon completion in 2014, it stood at 1,005 ft tall, making it the tallest residential building in the city for a few months until the completion of 432 Park Avenue.",
