        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "4ee2d115-9dc7-5693-96a9-f1bfa51a52e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Times Square, Manhattan, New York City, West 45th Street, Central Park\n- Buildings: Bertelsmann Building, 1540 Broadway, 432 Park Avenue, One57, Loew's State Theatre\n- Topics: office towers, residential skyscrapers, building heights, closures, completions\n\nFacts:\n- Loew's State Theatre in New York City closed on February 19, 1987, and the Bertelsmann Building was later built on its site.\n- The former Bertelsmann Building, now known as 1540 Broadway, is a 44-story, 733-foot office tower in Times Square in Manhattan, New York City, at West 45th Street.\n- In 2011, 432 Park Avenue was originally proposed at 1,300 feet.\n- One57 was completed in 2014 at 1,005 feet tall and became New York City's tallest residential building for a few months until 432 Park Avenue was completed.\n- 432 Park Avenue is a residential skyscraper in New York City overlooking Central Park.\n- 432 Park Avenue later topped out at 1,396 feet.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
